property_value: RO:0002175 NCBITaxon:9606
property_value: UBPROP:0000001 "When the splenic artery passes into the trabecula of the spleen and branches, they become known as the trabecular arteries. When these arteries then reach the white pulp, and become covered with Periarteriolar lymphoid sheaths, the name changes again to central arteries (or central arterioles). Branches of the central arteries are given to the red pulp, and these are called penicillar arteries).[Wikipedia]" xsd:string {ontology="Wikipedia", source="Wikipedia:Trabecular_arteries"}

